# um-texts 1
=== WEAPON Axe Adamantium
Adamantite axe
This weapon is very expensive - but it is worth it.

=== WEAPON Axe Bronze
Bronze axe
The simplest of metal axes. Do not rely on it too much.

=== WEAPON Axe Iron
Iron axe
This causes more damage than a bronze one. But there are better materials than iron.

=== WEAPON Axe Meteoric
Meteorite axe
In the hands of an experienced fighter, this can really make the enemy suffer...

=== WEAPON Axe Mithrill
Mithrill axe
Light, sharp, finely honed... and expensive.

=== WEAPON Axe Steel
Steel axe
This won't penetrate all types armor, but it can still be dangerous in the hands of an experienced fighter…

=== WEAPON Bad_Axe Bronze
Peasant's axe
With such an axe you can chop down trees. Or break it on yourself...

=== WEAPON Bad_Crossbow Bronze
Shattered crossbow
Can also be used in close quarters as a bludgeon - you won't feel bad about this thing.

=== WEAPON Bad_Dagger Bronze
Kitchen knife
You can use a knife like this to separate a hyena's ears from its head.

=== WEAPON Bad_Hammer Bronze
Baton
Perfect for shaking the dust out of carpets... ...and to beat reason into the heads of slaves.

=== WEAPON Bad_Short_Bow Bronze
Old bow
A good piece of equipment for the beginner archer, dreaming of becoming better at his craft.

=== WEAPON Bad_Spear Bronze
Bad pika
The name completely reflects its performance.

=== WEAPON Bad_Sword Bronze
An unbalanced sword
You can't fight with a sword like that for very long!

=== WEAPON Battle_Axe Adamantium
Adamantite battle axe
This is worth the price and good enough for serious fighting.

=== WEAPON Battle_Axe Bronze
Bronze battle axe
This is not much better than a simple bronze axe.

=== WEAPON Battle_Axe Iron
Iron battle axe
There are better materials than this - if you can afford them, of course.

=== WEAPON Battle_Axe Meteoric
Meteorite battle axe
You would be hard pressed to find armor which would withstand this axe, even in the coffers of kings.

=== WEAPON Battle_Axe Mithrill
Mithrill battle axe
Really good... And the price is appropriate.

=== WEAPON Battle_Axe Steel
Steel battle axe
This one is not bad at all! Though your opponent may have even better armor...

=== WEAPON Bone_Club Burned_Bones
Bone club (hard bone)
A good instrument to use on alone Orc.

=== WEAPON Bone_Club Decayed_Bones
Bone club (thin bone)
A club is a club.

=== WEAPON Bone_Club Dragon_Black_Bones
Bone club (Blue Dragon bone)
Perfect for charging with a spell!

=== WEAPON Bone_Club Dragon_Green_Bones
Bone club (Green Dragon bone)
No one can ignore a tap from this!

=== WEAPON Bone_Club Dragon_Red_Bones
Bone club (Red Dragon bone)
Now you definitely cannot call this just a club...

=== WEAPON Bone_Club Dry_Bones
Bone club (tough bone)
Using this, you could deal with a Goblin, but do not be so sure with an Orc!

=== WEAPON Bone_Club Scrab_Bones
Bone club (shell bone)
Shell bone is a good material for all kinds of weapons.

=== WEAPON Bone_Crossbow Burned_bones
Bone crossbow (thick bone)
If you're low on cash, it's fun to shoot yourself with this mechanical toy.

=== WEAPON Bone_Crossbow Decayed_bones
Bone crossbow (thin bone)
The making of a crossbow is an art by Gipath standards, and to use thin bone for it is insane.
=== WEAPON Bone_Crossbow Dragon_Black_Bones
Bone Crossbow (Blue Dragon Bone)
You won't find a better crossbow on Gipath.

=== WEAPON Bone_Crossbow Dragon_Green_Bones
Bone Crossbow (Green Dragon Bone)
You will have to pay very big money for this great weapon.

=== WEAPON Bone_Crossbow Dragon_Red_Bones
Bone crossbow (red dragon bone)
The troll would be frightened.

=== WEAPON Bone_Crossbow Dry_bones
Bone crossbow (strong bone)
A great weapon and a poor material.

=== WEAPON Bone_Crossbow Scrab_bones
Bone crossbow (petrified bone)
Not the worst combination of price and quality.

=== WEAPON Bone_Dagger Burned_bones
Bone knife (thick bone)
It's okay to start with.
=== WEAPON Bone_Dagger Decayed_bones
Bone knife (thin bone)
A bone knife is better than a stone knife, but the material was chosen extremely poorly in this case.
=== WEAPON Bone_Dagger Dragon_Black_Bones
Bone knife (blue dragon bone)
The best knife on Gipath.
=== WEAPON Bone_Dagger Dragon_Green_Bones
Bone Knife (Green Dragon Bone)
A real combat knife.

=== WEAPON Bone_Dagger Dragon_Red_Bones
Bone knife (red dragon bone)
Such a knife is a sign of high rank in society.
=== WEAPON Bone_Dagger Dry_bones
Bone knife (strong bone)
A little better than a knife made of thin bone.

=== WEAPON Bone_Dagger Scrab_bones
Bone knife (petrified bone)
With this knife, don't be afraid to go after a black boar.

=== WEAPON Bone_Long_Bow Burned_Bones
Long bone bow (hard bone)
An improvement on a dry bone bow.

=== WEAPON Bone_Long_Bow Decayed_Bones
Long bone bow (thin bone)
Good enough for training or hunting.

=== WEAPON Bone_Long_Bow Dragon_Black_Bones
Long bone bow (Blue Dragon bone)
A remarkable material put to good use!

=== WEAPON Bone_Long_Bow Dragon_Green_Bones
Long bone bow (Green Dragon bone)
Few other bone bows can compare with this one!

=== WEAPON Bone_Long_Bow Dragon_Red_Bones
Long bone bow (Red Dragon bone)
One of the best kinds of long bone bows.

=== WEAPON Bone_Long_Bow Dry_Bones
Long bone bow (tough bone)
Not the worst option, but there are better weapons than this!

=== WEAPON Bone_Long_Bow Scrab_Bones
Long bone bow (shell bone)
Not a bad thing to have with you when you go for a walk!

=== WEAPON Bone_Short_Bow Burned_Bones
Short bone bow (hard bone)
Arrows shot from this one are dangerous and not just for Goblins!

=== WEAPON Bone_Short_Bow Decayed_Bones
Short bone bow (thin bone)
Not a bad weapon, but some enemies will not even notice it....

=== WEAPON Bone_Short_Bow Dragon_Black_Bones
Short bone bow (Blue Dragon bone)
Impossible to find a better bone bow - except for the ones infused with magic.

=== WEAPON Bone_Short_Bow Dragon_Green_Bones
Short bone bow (Green Dragon bone)
In a different league altogether...

=== WEAPON Bone_Short_Bow Dragon_Red_Bones
Short bone bow (Red Dragon bone)
One of the best kinds of bone bows.

=== WEAPON Bone_Short_Bow Dry_Bones
Short bone bow (tough bone)
Better than a simple bow, but you should think about trying a more decent material...

=== WEAPON Bone_Short_Bow Scrab_Bones
Short bone bow (shell bone)
No one is going to like being hit by arrows shot from this bow.

=== WEAPON Bone_Spear Burned_Bones
Bone spear (hard bone)
Not a bad weapon against Goblins... but that's it.

=== WEAPON Bone_Spear Decayed_Bones
Bone spear (thin bone)
Much lighter than stone spears -  about all you can say for it.

=== WEAPON Bone_Spear Dragon_Black_Bones
Bone spear (Blue Dragon bone)
The only way to better a Dragon bone spear is to infuse it with a powerful spell...

=== WEAPON Bone_Spear Dragon_Green_Bones
Bone spear (Green Dragon bone)
A Dragon bone spear is a good thing. A magical one is even better.

=== WEAPON Bone_Spear Dragon_Red_Bones
Bone spear (Red Dragon bone)
A spear made of Dragon bone is a decent weapon. A magician could make it better still.

=== WEAPON Bone_Spear Dry_Bones
Bone spear (tough bone)
This is sharper than one made of thin bone; but maybe you should get something better?

=== WEAPON Bone_Spear Scrab_Bones
Bone spear (shell bone)
Now this is something serious.

=== WEAPON Cheat_Dagger Adamantium
Ritual adamantite knife
This metal is far too expensive to waste on trifles like this!

=== WEAPON Cheat_Dagger Bronze
Ritual bronze knife
Yes... you should start looking for something more serious as soon as possible...

=== WEAPON Cheat_Dagger Iron
Ritual iron knife
Iron, bronze - not much difference really.

=== WEAPON Cheat_Dagger Meteoric
Ritual meteorite knife
Is meteorite iron really so cheap you would waste it like this?

=== WEAPON Cheat_Dagger Mithrill
Ritual mithrill knife
One could find a better use for mithrill!

=== WEAPON Cheat_Dagger Steel
Ritual steel knife
Looks exquisite, but it is not much use.

=== WEAPON Crash_Axe Bronze
A sharpened axe
You can chase rats with this axe.

=== WEAPON Crash_Crossbow Bronze
An old crossbow
Pierces leather armor from a hundred paces away.

=== WEAPON Crash_Dagger Bronze
Dagger
For starters, it can be alright.

=== WEAPON Crash_Short_Bow Bronze
The wrong bow
It's already better value for money.

=== WEAPON Crash_Spear Bronze
Light spade
Not the worst weapon for a novice.

=== WEAPON Crash_Sword Bronze
Broken sword
A good sword, if not for the fact that it is broken and hastily forged.

=== WEAPON Crossbow Adamantium
Adamantite crossbow
With this one in your hands, you can afford to be a bit impolite.

=== WEAPON Crossbow Bronze
Bronze crossbow
Do not expect too much of a bronze crossbow.

=== WEAPON Crossbow Iron
Iron crossbow
Like any other iron item, this crossbow is better than the bronze but worse than the steel.

=== WEAPON Crossbow Meteoric
Meteorite crossbow
About the only way to improve on it is to add an extra spring.

=== WEAPON Crossbow Mithrill
Mithrill crossbow
A strong and long-range weapon. Go for it!

=== WEAPON Crossbow Steel
Steel crossbow
Bolts shot from a steel crossbow pierce even very good armor.

=== WEAPON Crystal_Axe Diamond
Diamond axe
The only thing better than a diamond weapon is a diamond weapon infused with magic...

=== WEAPON Crystal_Crossbow Diamond
Diamond crossbow
This does not come cheap: but a bolt shot from this crossbow will pierce any kind of armor at all.

=== WEAPON Crystal_Dagger Diamond
Diamond dagger
A stab with a diamond dagger is as fatal as a lightning strike!

=== WEAPON Crystal_Mace Diamond
Diamond mace
Even meteorite iron will not resist its blows!

=== WEAPON Crystal_Short_Bow Diamond
Diamond short bow
You should keep a bow like this next to the crown jewels!

=== WEAPON Crystal_Spear Diamond
Diamond spear
No armor will resist a diamond spear!

=== WEAPON Crystal_Sword Diamond
Diamond sword
A whole crystal sword is as awesome in combat as it is beautiful in your hand.

=== WEAPON Curved_Dagger Adamantium
Adamantine dirk
This one is a weapon for serious combat, not for an alehouse brawl!

=== WEAPON Curved_Dagger Bronze
Bronze dirk
More reliable than a simple dagger, lighter than a sword. But try for something better...

=== WEAPON Curved_Dagger Iron
Iron dirk
Not the worst possible dirk, but a lot worse than a steel one!

=== WEAPON Curved_Dagger Meteoric
Meteorite dirk
The very best! But the price, of course, tends to scare one off...

=== WEAPON Curved_Dagger Mithrill
Mithrill dirk
Light, sharp, finely honed... and expensive.

=== WEAPON Curved_Dagger Steel
Steel dirk
A serious weapon in the hands of an experienced warrior...

=== WEAPON Dagger Adamantium
Adamantite dagger
One of the best daggers available on this world.

=== WEAPON Dagger Bronze
Bronze dagger
The best way to kill with this is to stab your enemy in the back.

=== WEAPON Dagger Iron
Iron dagger
Modest....both in terms of price and quality.

=== WEAPON Dagger Meteoric
Meteorite dagger
Causes maximum damage possible. To achieve more, you would need a magician, not a blacksmith.

=== WEAPON Dagger Mithrill
Mithrill dagger
A light and sharp dagger. Expensive, but worth it.

=== WEAPON Dagger Steel
Steel dagger
A steel dagger is a worthy weapon! But steel cannot get through all kinds of armor.

=== WEAPON Hammer Adamantium
Adamantite battle hammer
An exotic weapon. One does not often come across something like this!

=== WEAPON Hammer Bronze
Bronze battle hammer
Good enough for training, but try not to use this if you get into serious trouble!

=== WEAPON Hammer Iron
Iron battle hammer
In an "iron on iron" fight, this will be good enough.

=== WEAPON Hammer Meteoric
Meteorite battle hammer
Makes an unforgettable impression on your enemies...

=== WEAPON Hammer Mithrill
Mithrill battle hammer
One can find better uses for mithrill than simply smashing heads with it...

=== WEAPON Hammer Steel
Steel battle hammer
Many would have to take this one seriously!

=== WEAPON His_Dagger Steel
Hysa knife
Great knife.

=== WEAPON Long_Bow Adamantium
Long adamantite bow
Not every warrior can wear armor capable of withstanding arrows from this bow.

=== WEAPON Long_Bow Bronze
Long bronze bow
A long bow is better than a short one. But think about obtaining better material....

=== WEAPON Long_Bow Iron
Long iron bow
Not a bad weapon if you want to shoot somebody in the back.

=== WEAPON Long_Bow Meteoric
Long meteorite bow
Would you like something better still? Forget it, this is the best!

=== WEAPON Long_Bow Mithrill
Long mithrill bow
An arrow shot from this bow hurts a lot more than the sting of a hornet!

=== WEAPON Long_Bow Steel
Long steel bow
An opponent armed with this one is a worthy enemy.

=== WEAPON Long_Crossbow Adamantium
Heavy adamantite crossbow
A long-range and powerful weapon - one of the most awesome on this world.

=== WEAPON Long_Crossbow Bronze
Heavy bronze crossbow
An extra spring will never hurt, even with a bronze crossbow.

=== WEAPON Long_Crossbow Iron
Heavy iron crossbow
Not the most awesome of crossbows... but do not write it off yet.

=== WEAPON Long_Crossbow Meteoric
Heavy meteorite crossbow
An arrow shot from this one will cut through adamantite armor like a steel needle cuts through paper!

=== WEAPON Long_Crossbow Mithrill
Heavy mithrill crossbow
Tough and flexible mithrill is an excellent material for crossbows.

=== WEAPON Long_Crossbow Steel
Heavy steel crossbow
A good weapon!

=== WEAPON Long_Spear Adamantium
Long adamantite spear
A very good weapon. And costs very good money.

=== WEAPON Long_Spear Bronze
Long bronze spear
Better than a simple bronze spear, but that is small comfort...

=== WEAPON Long_Spear Iron
Long iron spear
Not the best of long spears, but not the most expensive either.

=== WEAPON Long_Spear Meteoric
Long meteorite spear
Absolutely the best!

=== WEAPON Long_Spear Mithrill
Long mithrill spear
The material and the quality are most impressive; certainly worth the price!

=== WEAPON Long_Spear Steel
Long steel spear
This one would fend many an opponent off...

=== WEAPON Long_Sword Adamantium
Adamantite long sword
Even a less than experienced fighter could win a serious battle with this one!

=== WEAPON Long_Sword Bronze
Bronze long sword
A bronze sword is fine if your opponent forgot to get good armor.

=== WEAPON Long_Sword Iron
Iron long sword
This causes more damage than a bronze one, but it cannot pierce many types of armor.

=== WEAPON Long_Sword Meteoric
Meteorite long sword
No blacksmith could make a better long sword!

=== WEAPON Long_Sword Mithrill
Mithrill long sword
Expensive, but worth it!

=== WEAPON Long_Sword Steel
Steel long sword
A serious weapon in the hands of an experienced fighter...

=== WEAPON Mace Adamantium
Adamantite mace
With a heavy item like this in your hand, you can take on anything.

=== WEAPON Mace Bronze
Bronze mace
Inexpensive but impressive. At least in terms of appearance.

=== WEAPON Mace Iron
Iron mace
Not as nice looking as a bronze one, but it will cause greater damage.

=== WEAPON Mace Meteoric
Meteorite mace
The only thing better than a meteorite mace is a spiked meteorite mace.

=== WEAPON Mace Mithrill
Mithrill mace
A most serious weapon. And not cheap either.

=== WEAPON Mace Steel
Steel mace
The heaviness of the steel makes the blows extra powerful!

=== WEAPON New_Bow Diamond
Diamond bow
An arrow released from this bow can pierce through any chain mail.

=== WEAPON Saber Adamantium
Adamantite sabre
You could win a serious fight with this one!

=== WEAPON Saber Bronze
Bronze sabre
Do not rely too much on a bronze blade, although it is a little better than stone.

=== WEAPON Saber Iron
Iron sabre
Not bad, but nothing special.

=== WEAPON Saber Meteoric
Meteorite sabre
This blade will ensure at least a half victory.

=== WEAPON Saber Mithrill
Mithrill sabre
This one is definitely not for beginners!

=== WEAPON Saber Steel
Steel sabre
A serious weapon in the hands of an experienced fighter... but it will not pierce every kind of armor!

=== WEAPON Short_Bow Adamantium
Short adamantite bow
The springy adamantite makes this short bow an awesome weapon!

=== WEAPON Short_Bow Bronze
Short bronze bow
Metal gives bows additional properties - but bronze is not the most flexible of metals...

=== WEAPON Short_Bow Iron
Short iron bow
Wave away an arrow shot from this bow, if you can!

=== WEAPON Short_Bow Meteoric
Short meteorite bow
If you see that your enemy has this bow, make a will.

=== WEAPON Short_Bow Mithrill
Short mithrill bow
Even a very well-protected opponent will have to take the owner of this one seriously.

=== WEAPON Short_Bow Steel
Short steel bow
Steel makes arrows quicker and more precise.

=== WEAPON Spear Adamantium
Adamantite spear
A very good weapon. And costs very good money.

=== WEAPON Spear Bronze
Bronze spear
The simplest metal spear. Not the worst weapon...

=== WEAPON Spear Iron
Iron spear
Not the best weapon, but not the most expensive either.

=== WEAPON Spear Meteoric
Meteorite spear
Only meteorite armor could withstand this....and that's a big maybe...

=== WEAPON Spear Mithrill
Mithrill spear
The material speaks for itself!

=== WEAPON Spear Steel
Steel spear
Now this is something efficient, and not too expensive.

=== WEAPON Spiked_Club Adamantium
Adamantite heavy spiked mace
This is capable of breaking any skull!

=== WEAPON Spiked_Club Bronze
Heavy bronze spiked mace
You can't make a good spiked mace out of bronze...

=== WEAPON Spiked_Club Iron
Heavy iron spiked mace
Of course iron is better than bronze but poorer than all the other metals...

=== WEAPON Spiked_Club Meteoric
Meteorite heavy spiked mace
The blacksmiths did all they could. Now it is the turn of the magicians.

=== WEAPON Spiked_Club Mithrill
Mithrill heavy spiked mace
With an argument like this in your hands, you are well-placed to claim the right to go first...

=== WEAPON Spiked_Club Steel
Steel heavy spiked mace
A good weapon for one about to embark on a dangerous voyage.

=== WEAPON Spiked_Mace Adamantium
Adamantite spiked mace
Good things do not come cheap.

=== WEAPON Spiked_Mace Bronze
Heavy bronze mace
A spiked bronze mace - you can only weight it more.

=== WEAPON Spiked_Mace Iron
Heavy iron mace
Iron is not the best material for spikes, but this mace is heavier than a regular one.

=== WEAPON Spiked_Mace Meteoric
Meteorite spiked mace
After a blow with this mace, you can use the armor of your opponent as a sieve!

=== WEAPON Spiked_Mace Mithrill
Mithrill spiked mace
Even steel armor will not resist mithrill spikes.

=== WEAPON Spiked_Mace Steel
Heavy steel mace
Steel doesn't make good spikes, but a mace is a formidable weapon anyway.

=== WEAPON Stone_Axe Granite
Granite axe
Better than stone - you could even cut some wood... with difficulty.

=== WEAPON Stone_Axe Malachite
Obsidian axe
You might even cut yourself with this axe!

=== WEAPON Stone_Axe Rock
Stone axe
The simplest of axes. More of a club than an axe, really...

=== WEAPON Stone_Axe Silicon
Silicon axe
Silicon is a step forward - at least you can cut with it.

=== WEAPON Stone_Battle_Axe Granite
Granite battle axe
Better than a stone battle axe - but, alas, not much better!

=== WEAPON Stone_Battle_Axe Malachite
Obsidian battle axe
This axe will make your opponent respect you.

=== WEAPON Stone_Battle_Axe Rock
Stone battle axe
This is not just a stone tied to a stick, but not far off it....

=== WEAPON Stone_Battle_Axe Silicon
Silicon battle axe
Now you can really rely on this one (provided your opponent is not too strong).

=== WEAPON Stone_Battle_Sword Granite
Granite battle sword
With this weapon you can successfully fight goblins.
=== WEAPON Stone_Battle_Sword Malachite
Obsidian battle sword
The best sword on Gipath.

=== WEAPON Stone_Battle_Sword Rock
Stone Battle Sword
This weapon is quite good, but the material chosen for it is unfortunate.

=== WEAPON Stone_Battle_Sword Silicon
Flint combat sword
Not a bad weapon, well worth the price.
=== WEAPON Stone_Battle_hammer Granite
Heavy granite hammer
Looks a bit better and is a little bit more efficient than a stone one - and only a little bit.....

=== WEAPON Stone_Battle_hammer Malachite
Heavy obsidian hammer
This is a heavy one! Only metal hammers are better.

=== WEAPON Stone_Battle_hammer Rock
Heavy stone hammer
The heavier the stone, the greater the damage...

=== WEAPON Stone_Battle_hammer Silicon
Heavy silicon hammer
The sharp silicon edges cause additional damage to the enemy.

=== WEAPON Stone_Dagger Granite
Granite dagger
Could be useful at the start, but do not rely on it too much.

=== WEAPON Stone_Dagger Malachite
Obsidian dagger
A good piercing weapon - the best of stone daggers.

=== WEAPON Stone_Dagger Rock
Stone dagger
Almost worthless, both in terms of price and efficiency.

=== WEAPON Stone_Dagger Silicon
Silicon dagger
Not a bad piercing weapon - efficient and not too expensive.

=== WEAPON Stone_Formatter_drive_C Rock
Rock drive C: formatter
As a matter of fact you will NEVER see this item. Oh, do you really see it??? Well then, try to guess what will happen next!

=== WEAPON Stone_Hammer Granite
Granite hammer
Good enough for starters.

=== WEAPON Stone_Hammer Malachite
Obsidian hammer
Sufficient to break a Goblin's head with the first blow!

=== WEAPON Stone_Hammer Rock
Stone hammer
Would come in very handy both in the smithy and in a fight...

=== WEAPON Stone_Hammer Silicon
Silicon hammer
One way to equip an inexperienced fighter.

=== WEAPON Stone_Short_Bow Granite
Bow (granite head arrows)
The shortcomings are many, but it is still better than nothing.

=== WEAPON Stone_Short_Bow Malachite
Bow (obsidian head arrows)
Causes the maximum damage possible with this kind of weapon.

=== WEAPON Stone_Short_Bow Rock
Bow (stone head arrows)
Your chances of hitting the target are not great, but this bow can still shoot arrows.

=== WEAPON Stone_Short_Bow Silicon
Bow (silicon head arrows)
Now you can risk going beyond the gates, and maybe you will even get back!

=== WEAPON Stone_Spear Granite
Granite head spear
Granite is better than stone ... but worse than any other material.

=== WEAPON Stone_Spear Malachite
Obsidian head spear
Now this does look like a real spear...

=== WEAPON Stone_Spear Rock
Stone head spear
The cheapest, most simple spear.

=== WEAPON Stone_Spear Silicon
Silicon head spear
Silicon heads are much sharper than other stone ones...

=== WEAPON Stone_Sword Granite
Granite sword
Better than simple stone, but not by much.

=== WEAPON Stone_Sword Malachite
Obsidian sword
Only metal swords are better than those made of obsidian.

=== WEAPON Stone_Sword Rock
Stone sword
You should try to trade it for something more serious.

=== WEAPON Stone_Sword Silicon
Silicon sword
You can definitely do some damage with this sword.

=== WEAPON Thief_Axe Bronze
Thieves' axe
It's good to learn on such an axe, but for combat it's not the best option.
=== WEAPON Thief_Crossbow Bronze
Thieving Crossbow
With a crossbow like this, you can kill a troll by hitting it in the forehead!

=== WEAPON Thief_Dagger Bronze
Thief's dagger
If money is no object, you won't find a better knife.
=== WEAPON Thief_Short_Bow Bronze
Thief's bow
Thief bows are used by the most experienced hunters.

=== WEAPON Thief_Spear Bronze
Thieves' Spike
Although its damage is low, it can be used for support.

=== WEAPON Thief_Sword Bronze
Thieving sword
With such a sword, you can prove to a young ogre that sometimes food is wormy.

=== WEAPON Unique_Spear Mithrill
"Lethal Lightning" spear
A unique weapon. Brother Blacksmith is not up to making anything comparable.

=== WEAPON Unique_Sword Steel
Ancient sword
A unique ancient weapon. No one can deconstruct it or make another one like it nowadays.

